IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il40-nouns`

-- Section 4 (language): (a) Hebrew is the language of the State; (b) Arabic has a special status, and the regulation of its use in or
-- before State institutions "shall be in law"; (c) the section does not harm "the status given in practice" to Arabic before the
-- Basic Law "came into force".  Row IL-40.  SEAT: the individual (NOTES.md section 1).
--
-- WHAT THE OFFICIAL TEXT DOES NOT SAY (read from the page image of Sefer HaChukim 2743 p. 898, NOTES.md section 4):
--   * s 4(c) names no enactment.  Every "ראו ..." pointer in the consolidation is the consolidator's editorial note, not the Law's.
--   * s 4(c) speaks of the status given IN PRACTICE (בפועל), not of a status given by an enactment.
--   * the Basic Law has no commencement section, so "before [its] commencement" has no day in the text.
-- Each of these is an input or a named reading here (forks F1, F2), default declined, never a guess.

§ `Section 4`

§§ `Section 4(a) and (b): the status the Basic Law gives`

-- bl:28 | עברית היא שפת המדינה.
-- bl:29 | לשפה הערבית מעמד מיוחד במדינה; הסדרת השימוש בשפה הערבית במוסדות ממלכתיים או בפניהם תהיה בחוק.
@ref Basic Law s 4(a), (b); Sefer HaChukim 5778 no. 2743 p. 898
GIVEN lang IS A `A language`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A status the Basic Law gives to a language`
`the status the Basic Law gives to` lang MEANS
    CONSIDER lang
        WHEN Hebrew             THEN JUST `the language of the State`
        WHEN Arabic             THEN JUST `a special status in the State`
        WHEN English            THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `Another language` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Section 4(b): "shall be in law" and the Interpretation Law's word for "law"`

-- Interpretation Law 5741-1981 s 3 (carried from the aid, aids/interpretation-law-5741-1981.he.wiki.txt):
-- il:39 | ”חוק“ – חוק של הכנסת או פקודה;
-- il:41 | ”חיקוק“ – חוק או תקנה;
-- il:54 | ”פקודה“ – פקודה שניתנה לפני הקמת המדינה או פקודה של מועצת המדינה הזמנית;
-- Order in Council: s 3 lists "דבר המלך במועצתו" under "דין" (para (3)(a), quoted next), apart from "חוק".  An Order in Council is therefore a "דין" and not a "חוק" (fork F4).
-- il:35 | אקט של הפרלמנט הבריטי או דבר המלך במועצתו או חלק מהם, או תקנות לפיהם, ודיני המשפט המקובל ועקרוני היושר של אנגליה, כפי תקפם במדינה;
@ref Basic Law s 4(b); Interpretation Law s 3 definitions of "חוק", "חיקוק", "פקודה"; NOTES.md fork F4
GIVEN kind IS A `A kind of enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(b) counts as law an instrument of the kind` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `a law of the Knesset`                                                                      THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a Basic Law`                                                                               THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an Ordinance given before the State was established or by the Provisional Council of State` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an Order in Council of the Mandate`                                                        THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a regulation`                                                                              THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a decision of the Government`                                                              THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an administrative direction`                                                               THEN FALSE

§§ `Section 4(c): what was held before the Basic Law`

-- The provisions the bundle shows as giving Arabic a standing before the Basic Law, as typed values.
-- Article 82 (read from the page image of Laws of Palestine vol. 3 p. 2759; the amending instruments of 1939 and 5708 are not in the bundle).
-- order:363 | כל הפקודות, המודעות הרשמיות והטפסים הרשמיים של הממשלה וכל המודעות הרשמיות של רשויות מקומיות ועיריות בתחומים שייקבעו עפ״י צו מאת הממשלה יפורסמו בערבית ובעברית. בהתחשב עם כל תקנות שתתקין הממשלה אפשר להשתמש בשלש השפות במשרדי הממשלה ובבתי המשפט.
-- order:364 | אם תהא כל סתירה בין הנוסח האנגלי של כל פקודה או מודעה רשמית או טופס רשמי לבין הנוסח הערבי או העברי שלהם, הולכין אחר הנוסח האנגלי.
-- Law and Administration Ordinance 5708-1948 s 15(b) (read from the page image of Iton Rishmi no. 2, Supplement A, 21.5.1948, p. 3).
-- ord:120 | כל הוראה בחוק הדורשת את השמוש בשפה האנגלית, בטלה.
@ref Palestine Order in Council 1922 art 82; read from the page image, Laws of Palestine vol. 3 p. 2759
`art 82 of the Palestine Order in Council 1922` MEANS `A provision that gave Arabic a standing before the Basic Law` WITH
    `the instrument`            IS "דברי המלך במועצה על ארץ־ישראל, 1922 עד 1947"
    `the provision`             IS "82"
    `its kind`                  IS `an Order in Council of the Mandate`
    `what it does as to Arabic` IS "official ordinances, notices and forms are published in Arabic and Hebrew; the languages may be used in government offices and courts subject to regulations"
    `the Basic Law names it`    IS FALSE

@ref Law and Administration Ordinance 5708-1948 s 15(b); read from the page image, Iton Rishmi no. 2, Supplement A, p. 3
`s 15(b) of the Law and Administration Ordinance 5708-1948` MEANS `A provision that gave Arabic a standing before the Basic Law` WITH
    `the instrument`            IS "פקודת סדרי השלטון והמשפט, תש״ח–1948"
    `the provision`             IS "15(ב)"
    `its kind`                  IS `an Ordinance given before the State was established or by the Provisional Council of State`
    `what it does as to Arabic` IS "voids any provision of law requiring the use of English, which leaves article 82's Arabic and Hebrew; it gives Arabic no standing of its own"
    `the Basic Law names it`    IS FALSE

GIVETH A LIST OF `A provision that gave Arabic a standing before the Basic Law`
`the provisions the bundle shows as giving Arabic a standing before the Basic Law` MEANS
    LIST `art 82 of the Palestine Order in Council 1922`, `s 15(b) of the Law and Administration Ordinance 5708-1948`

-- The day of the Basic Law's commencement, by reading.  Passed: 19 July 2018 (official footnote, p. 898: "התקבל בכנסת ביום ז' באב התשע״ח (19 ביולי 2018)").
-- Published: 26 July 2018 (Sefer HaChukim 2743, 14 Av 5778).  No section of the Basic Law gives a commencement day.
@ref Sefer HaChukim 5778 no. 2743 p. 898 (cover and footnote); NOTES.md fork F2
GIVEN reading IS A `A reading of the day the Basic Law commenced`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the Basic Law commenced, reading it as` reading MEANS
    CONSIDER reading
        WHEN `the day it was passed`                  THEN JUST (Date 19 7 2018)
        WHEN `the day it was published`               THEN JUST (Date 26 7 2018)
        WHEN `the commencement day is declined`       THEN NOTHING

-- Interpretation Law s 21 fixes the HOUR of commencement (00:01 of the commencement day) and not the day.  At day level the commencement day
-- itself is therefore not answered either way.
-- il:124 | שעת תחילת תקפו של חיקוק היא בשעה 00.01 של יום תחילתו.
@ref Interpretation Law s 21; NOTES.md fork F2
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      commencement IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a status held on` day `was held before the commencement day` commencement MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF day LESS THAN commencement    THEN JUST TRUE
        IF day GREATER THAN commencement THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE                        NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the answer where` a `and` b `agree, and nothing where they differ` MEANS
    IF a EQUALS b THEN a ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      reading IS A `A reading of the day the Basic Law commenced`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a status held on` day `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` reading MEANS
    CONSIDER reading
        WHEN `the day it was passed`            THEN `a status held on` day `was held before the commencement day` (Date 19 7 2018)
        WHEN `the day it was published`         THEN `a status held on` day `was held before the commencement day` (Date 26 7 2018)
        WHEN `the commencement day is declined` THEN `the answer where` (`a status held on` day `was held before the commencement day` (Date 19 7 2018)) `and` (`a status held on` day `was held before the commencement day` (Date 26 7 2018)) `agree, and nothing where they differ`

-- Section 4(c) saves a status the way a "no harm" clause does: it says what it leaves unharmed and is silent on the rest, so a status
-- outside what it reaches, or held after the commencement day, is NOT answered "no" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c): a scope limit with no "only").
@ref Basic Law s 4(c); NOTES.md forks F1, F2
GIVEN status IS A `A status of Arabic held before the Basic Law`
      saving IS A `A reading of what s 4(c) saves`
      commencement IS A `A reading of the day the Basic Law commenced`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` status `, reading what it saves as` saving `and the commencement day as` commencement MEANS
    IF `a status held on` (status's `the day it was held`) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` commencement EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND (CONSIDER saving
                   WHEN `only a status given in practice`                                          THEN status's `it was given in practice`
                   WHEN `a status given in practice and a status an enactment gave`                THEN status's `it was given in practice` OR status's `an enactment gave it`
                   WHEN `what s 4(c) saves is declined`                                            THEN status's `it was given in practice`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
